      "Flat-band: $\\phi_s = 0$, $p_s = N_A, n_s = n_i^2/N_A$.",
      "Depletion: $0 < \\phi_s < \\phi_F$, $p_s > n_s$, minority electrons negligible.",
      "Midgap / Intrinsic condition: $\\phi_s = \\phi_F$, $n_s = p_s = n_i$.",
      "Weak Inversion: $\\phi_F < \\phi_s < 2\\phi_F$, $p_s < n_s < N_A$. Minority electrons outnumber holes at the surface, but remain far below background acceptor doping; depletion charge still dominates total space charge.",
      "Onset of Strong Inversion (Threshold condition): $\\phi_s = 2\\phi_F$, $n_s = N_A$, $p_s = n_i^2/N_A$. Surface electron concentration equals the bulk majority hole concentration.",
      "Strong Inversion: $\\phi_s > 2\\phi_F$, $n_s \\gg N_A$. Conductive electron inversion channel forms; surface band bending pins at $\\approx 2\\phi_F$; depletion width reaches maximum $x_{d,\\max} = \\sqrt{\\frac{4\\epsilon_{si}\\phi_F}{q N_A}}$.",
